# chat-starter — Project Context

Expo (React Native) chat starter with Firebase Auth, Firestore, and Storage. Targets iOS, Android, and web. Intended as an open-source starting point, not a full messenger.

## Key paths

- App routes: `app/` (expo-router)
- Firebase init: `lib/firebase.ts` (not `@/firebase` — collides with npm `firebase` package)
- Auth context: `context/auth.tsx`
- Data schema: `docs/SCHEMA.md` (canonical — do not drift from it)
- Setup (Firebase Console, deploy): `docs/SETUP.md`
- Roadmap: `docs/ROADMAP.md`

## AI vs human

| AI (repo) | Human (outside repo) |
|-----------|----------------------|
| App code, types, UX | Firebase Console: auth, indexes, publish rules |
| `firebase/*.rules` and `firebase/firestore.indexes.json` | `yarn deploy:rules` or paste into Console |
| `firebase.json`, `eas.json`, `.env.example` | Run `firebase deploy`, `eas build`, Apple accounts |
| Sync Firestore user docs from app | Authorized domains, own Firebase project |

Never commit `.env.local`, `.firebaserc`, or secrets. Use `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` for client Firebase config.

## Conventions

- Minimize scope; match existing StyleSheet patterns in each screen
- Real-time data: Firestore `onSnapshot` (see home + chat screens)
- Document ID for users = Auth `uid`
- Chat rooms: 1:1 only; `participants` is `string[]` of UIDs
